# Cross-origin isolation for the labeling app, so onnxruntime-web can use more
# than one WASM thread (issue #15). Everything the app loads — the ORT runtime,
# the model, Shoelace's assets — is same-origin, which is what require-corp
# needs.
#
# `/*` rather than the `/ui/*` this was scoped to: the app had the apex to
# itself only from `/ui/` down, and a rule on `/*` would have broken the landing
# page's cross-origin Google Fonts. The app now owns occupancy.rails49.org
# outright and the landing page lives on another origin, so there is nothing
# left here to leave alone (rails49/control#47).
#
# Lives in `ui/public/` so vite copies it to the root of `ui/dist/`, which is
# the directory `bin/deploy.sh` uploads. `ui/tests/publicDir.test.ts` names it.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
